          "text": "Prior pelvic ultrasound finding, per patient report"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Prior ultrasound reportedly showed a single intramural fibroid approximately 4.5 cm; no follow-up imaging since."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-8",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-8",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Menstrual history"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Menses regular every 28–30 days, lasting 6–7 days; first 2–3 days heavy. Uses super pads, changing every 2–3 hours on heavy days, with occasional small clots. No flooding through clothes or nocturnal sheet soaking. Patient feels bleeding may be a bit heavier this year but remains able to work and has not taken days off."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-9",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-9",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Menstrual and pelvic symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Mild dysmenorrhoea on days 1–2; uses ibuprofen 400 mg for 1–2 doses with good effect. Reports some pelvic fullness, especially around the period, with no constant pain."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-10",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-10",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Patient-reported associated symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Denies intermenstrual bleeding, postcoital bleeding, dyspareunia, dysuria, change in bowel habit, increased urinary frequency or urgency, shortness of breath, unusual exertional fatigue, dizziness, abnormal vaginal discharge, fever, night sweats, and weight loss."
      }
    },
